{
  "A booking on an earlier day is always reported as over, even when its 90-minute sitting runs past midnight. A 23:00 or 23:30 booking is reported over at 00:10 the next day, while the table is still held until 00:30 or 01:00. Callers that free the table or treat the guest as gone would act too early.": "right",
  "The availability loop iterates over `&slots[..slots.len() - 1]`, so the last week's slot is never checked. If the table is already booked in the final week (or for any single-week request), `handle` saves a double booking instead of returning `SlotTaken`, which breaks the all-or-nothing guarantee.": "right",
  "The check `input.party >= table.seats` refuses a party that exactly fills the table, so on a 4-seat table a party of 4 fails with PartyTooLarge (\"seats 4, not 4\"). It should be `>`. The tests only try 3 and 5, so the boundary is not covered.": "right",
  "The check filters bookings to the day, then also requires `existing.slot == input.slot`, and `Slot` includes the start time. A guest can therefore still book 19:00 and 21:00 on the same day, even though the failure reason and the test name `a_guest_may_book_once_a_day` say one booking per day. The check only catches the same guest at the same time on a different table, and the day filter does nothing.": "right",
  "The lower bound uses `<=` against 17:00, so a 17:00 booking is refused, yet the reason says bookings are taken from 17:00 to 21:30 and the upper bound 21:30 is inclusive. Guests asking for 17:00 get a refusal that contradicts its own message. The test checks only 16:30 and 17:30, so the boundary is untested.": "wrong",
  "`weeks` is only checked for zero, with no upper limit. A guest posting a huge `weeks` value (for example 4000000000) makes `handle` allocate a Vec of that many slots and probe each one, which can exhaust memory or hang the process. The limit should be a returned failure variant.": "right",
  "handle validates only first_moved; second_moved (moving onto the first booking's table) is saved without the party-size or slot-taken check. A party larger than the first table's seats, or a clash with a third booking at that slot, is silently saved.": "right",
  "weeks is only checked for zero, and the route parses it from the form as any u32. A guest sending a huge value such as 4294967295 makes handle allocate a vector of billions of slots and query the repository for each one, which can exhaust memory or hang the server. There is no upper bound and no failure variant for it.": "right"
}
